From 52108d05f4faff459b635a18b3c335a01307ccbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:40:19 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] fix(desktop): find PCAP jobs by name when Windows
 virtualizes AppData

Every PCAP upload answered 404 "Analysis job not found." when the app
was started from an MSIX-packaged app (the Claude desktop app, for one).
Windows then shows %APPDATA% through
...\Packages\<pkg>\LocalCache\Roaming, so a new job folder resolved
there while jobs_root resolved to the real Roaming path. The service
compared the two and rejected every job. The upload itself had
succeeded: input.pcap and state.json were written.

Job folders are now addressed by name. The id must match
^[0-9a-f]{32}$, which keeps the name inside jobs_root. _is_link_like()
refuses a folder that is a symlink, junction or other reparse point;
measured virtualized folders are none of these.

Startup recovery and expiry cleanup share one _job_dirs() enumerator
with the same rules. Recovery used to walk */state.json and could follow
a planted junction and rewrite a state.json outside jobs_root, a gap
that predates this change.

Tests (desktop/runtime/tests, stdlib unittest; 6/6 on Python 3.11 and
3.13):
- virtualization simulated by patching Path.resolve
- ids that are not 32 hex characters
- junctions under a job id and under any other name
- cleanup observed at rmtree itself
- four mutants of the fix are all caught

Against the ISO edition's real, virtualized jobs folder, lookups went
from 1/5 found to 5/5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
